    trap: 'On these data-skills items the scheme credits ONLY the correct finished value (the official answer is literally \'19 (%)\' for 6 marks). Stopping after writing out the two given percentages, subtracting the wrong way round, or doing the arithmetic but dropping the % so it isn\'t a valid figure, loses the mark. \'Calculate\' is not satisfied by quoting the numbers from the question — only the single correct difference, properly computed and labelled, scores.',
    source: 'LC Geography OL marking scheme 2025 (Part Three data-skills, % working population in selected EU countries 2023, part iii): \'Calculate the difference between the percentage of the male working population in employment and the percentage of the female working population in employment in Italy — 19 (%) 6m\' (table: Italy male 76%, female 57%)',
    marks: 6,
