    subjectId: 'french', subjectLabel: 'French', level: 'higher',
    questionRef: 'HL · Section A · Compréhension Écrite 1, Q2(b)',
    stem: 'Trouvez dans la deuxième section le mot qui veut dire « obtenir ».',
    commandWord: 'Trouvez',
    demand: '‘Trouvez … le mot qui veut dire …’ asks for ONE single word from the named section that is a synonym of the glossed word — and nothing else around it. The answer is a precise lexical pick (here the infinitive ‘Acquérir’). The same cue also appears as a grammar-spotting version, e.g. ‘Trouvez … un verbe au participe présent’ (2024 HL), where you must name the one word in the exact form asked for.',
    trap: 'Adding extra words around the target. The 2025 HL scheme gives the bare ‘Acquérir’ 5 marks but ‘D’acquérir’ — carrying the attached preposition — only 4, under the rule ‘Minus 1 Mark for each extraneous element’. With ‘Trouvez le mot’, the answer is exactly one clean word: copy in the article, preposition or neighbouring words and each extra element costs a mark. (For the grammar variant, e.g. ‘un verbe au participe présent’, only the word in the correct form is on the scheme’s accepted list — in 2024 HL ‘Portant’/‘Criant’ = 5 — so a word in the wrong tense or form earns nothing.)',
