    demand: 'This is a define-the-term cue: write one precise sentence capturing global interconnectedness/integration through trade and the international movement of goods, services, capital and technology. The scheme accepts e.g. \'the process by which the world is becoming increasingly interconnected as a result of massively increased trade and cultural exchange\' or \'the increasing internationalisation of markets\'. The full 6 marks go to a single complete definition statement, not a list of examples.',
    trap: '\'Explain the term\' here means DEFINE, not give reasons or impacts. Listing examples (multinationals, the internet, cheap flights) or describing causes/effects of globalisation instead of stating what the term MEANS leaves the definition award unearned. The scheme awards the 6 marks for a stand-alone meaning statement (interconnection/internationalisation of markets) — parts (ii) and (iii) are where reasons and impacts are rewarded, so spending your definition on those scores nothing here.',
