    questionRef: '2022 HL · Q15(b)(i)',
    stem: 'The graph below shows the Euro (€) to Pound Sterling (£) exchange rate, December 2012 to December 2021. Identify one period where the value of the Euro depreciates against the Pound Sterling. Explain your answer.',
    commandWord: 'Identify',
    demand: 'Two-stage award (4 + 4): first name a valid date range from the graph where the € weakens (the scheme accepts Dec 2013–Dec 2015, Dec 2018–Dec 2019, or Dec 2020–Dec 2021); then earn the explanation marks by reading the line — depreciation means fewer pence of Sterling can be bought per Euro (e.g. the €/£ rate falls from about 0.80 to 0.70), so the Euro buys less Sterling.',
    trap: 'Depreciation of the Euro against Sterling means the €/£ line FALLS (fewer £ per €) — students invert the axis and pick a period where the line rises, which is appreciation, and lose the 4 identification marks. Even with a correct period, the scheme withholds the second 4 marks unless you cite the graph movement (the rate declining from roughly 0.80 to 0.70) — naming a period with no graph-based explanation caps you at 4 of 8.',
    source: 'LC Economics 2022 HL marking scheme, Q15(b)(i) (period award + "the amount of Sterling which can be bought per Euro declines from 0.80 pence to 0.70 pence approximately" — 4 + 4 = 8 marks)',
