    trap: 'This is an all-or-nothing single-statement question. The scheme gives exactly one model sentence with no partial-credit ladder - there is no separate award for naming only one of the two flows. Get the direction wrong, define a deficit (expenditure exceeds revenue) instead, reverse the inequality, or describe the capital or overall budget rather than the CURRENT budget, and it counts as an \'Incorrect answer\', which the scheme marks at 0. So all 12 marks ride on the exact \'current revenue exceeds current expenditure\' relationship; a vaguely-right gesture at one side is not worth half the marks.',
